:name: WS500-OpenFW whole-firmware emulation
:description: Boots the WS500 open firmware on an emulated STM32F072RB (PROJECT_PLAN §8.2).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Interactive use:   renode renode/ws500-openfw.resc
#                    (then inspect with `sysbus.cpu PC`, `logLevel`, etc.)
# Automated use:     renode-test renode/ws500.robot   (that .robot replicates
#                    this setup so it can start emulation under a Log Tester).
#
# The firmware ELF path can be overridden before include, e.g.:
#   renode -e "$elf=@/abs/path/ws500-openfw.elf; include @renode/ws500-openfw.resc"
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Default ELF location = CI/CMake build output, relative to the repo root.
$elf?=@build/ws500-openfw.elf

using sysbus

mach create "ws500"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @renode/ws500f072.repl

# Debug/link build keeps the .symtab function symbols LoadELF needs for the
# liveness hooks (main, ctrl_tick, board_init, field_drive_set, Error_Handler).
sysbus LoadELF $elf

# --- Optional instrumentation (commented; enable interactively as needed) ---
# Log every entry into the 10 ms control loop and the fatal handler:
#   sysbus.cpu LogFunctionNames true "ctrl_tick Error_Handler"
# ...or the PROJECT_PLAN §7 R3 fault path (what renode/ws500.robot watches):
#   sysbus.cpu LogFunctionNames true "ctrl_tick enter_safe_state fault_nmi_stage2 fault_hardfault_stage2 Error_Handler"
#
# --- Reproducing the fault test by hand -------------------------------------
# The §7 R3 path ends in NVIC_SystemReset(), and a Cortex-M0 re-fetches SP/PC
# from address 0 — which the stock platform does not map. Add the BOOT0=0 flash
# mirror BEFORE LoadELF above, exactly as ws500.robot does, or the CPU halts
# instead of rebooting:
#   sysbus Unregister sysbus.flash
#   machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString "flash: Memory.MappedMemory @ { sysbus 0x08000000; sysbus 0x00000000 } { size: 0x20000 }"
# Then, with the machine running, inject a fault by pending NMI:
#   pause; sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0xE000ED04 0x80000000; start
# Watch the field-PWM timer and ADC being configured:
#   sysbus LogPeripheralAccess sysbus.timer1 true
#   sysbus LogPeripheralAccess sysbus.adc true

# --- INA226 sensor stub ---
# Renode ships no INA226 model; the firmware tolerates an absent device via a
# 5 ms HAL I2C timeout. If/when a model is added, attach it here, e.g.:
#   machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString "ina226: Sensors.<Model> @ i2c1 0x40"

# Start emulation (interactive). renode-test does NOT include this file, so it
# controls start timing itself; this line only affects the interactive path.
start
